''               attended screen uses; STOP is live whenever a wheel can move; the countdown carries a label;
''               a heartbeat dot blinks while cog 0 runs; end screens wait for START. BM-PLAN's finds for FLOOR
''               and UICHECK corrected (PL-65). No record changes shape; WHY gains OPERATOR_STOP, so FMT stays 3
''               17 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=13, FMT 4: the Visit 4 cells for the 6.0.0 driver work (task 3560).
''               New part D (-D DUAL_PART_D, tier dual-d): the STEERSEG and LIMIT segments, which certify the
''               front cog's contract (e-stop latch, ordered stop, cooperative shutdown, tracking reset, time
''               stop, lockstep, loop health) and current limiting (fold-back, derate, the protective stop),
''               through the steering object and one wheel. Every motion part now measures LAGBOUND, the
''               instrument's own running max |err| (the lag limiter's invariant: the unfixed driver saturates
''               the field at 127). Part B gains STOPCUR and RAMPDROOP on the FAULTB trials, the OVERSHT
''               stop-limit band and the DDU_M cross-check, and a fault-API trial provoked by a 180-degree
''               offset with the PL-66 same-power retry after it. Part C gains the STOPDECEL no-regression
''               reading; part A gains NOFOLD. New records BM-STOPCUR, BM-DISTM, BM-LAG, BM-FRONTST,
''               BM-LIMST and BM-DSTEP; BM-FLTAPI gains the retry fields. The record set grows, so FMT goes
''               to 4 the way it went to 3
''               17 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=14, FMT 5: the Visit 4 REPAIR CYCLE (task 3563). Every change is to
''               this harness or to a criterion; no driver defect was found. PL-76/PL-29: no dispatch helper
''               selects between two METHOD CALLS with `? :` any more -- a ternary runs both branches, so
''               eleven sites commanded or queried the wheel they were not addressing, and five of the Visit
''               4 error lines were the never-started wheelR answering. PL-83: TIMESTOP waited D_REST_MS for
''               a stop only due D_TIMESTOP_MS later, and judged rest against a bound smaller than
''               waitRest()'s own confirmation dwell; both are computed now. PL-79: NOFOLD splits into
''               NOFOLD (no derate) and the new RATELAW cell, whose band carries the rung's own tick
''               quantisation. PL-80: DERATE judges derated-and-restored, and the underivable arrival-time
''               window is deleted. PL-82: STOPCUR judges a FIXED bound, not a hold reference that drifts
''               with motor temperature, and BM-STOPCUR gains hold_pk_mV and bound_mV. PL-78: LAGBOUND's
''               bound is the driver's own fault test, and BM-LAG gains hold and fault. PL-77: BM-DISTM's
''               ticks are a live read beside the metres and the conversion is signed. PL-84: BM-DISTM
''               also gains str_mm_x100, the STEERING object's own travel-per-tick read back through the
''               new testGetTickInMM() -- at Visit 4 that copy held about -544_643, which refused every
''               driveForDistance() in the segment with ERR_LIMIT_UNRESOLVABLE while the record printed
''               the MOTOR object's healthy 576; the DISTM cell now fails when the two copies differ.
''               Three records gain fields and the cell set gains one, so FMT goes to 5
''               17 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=15, FMT 6: task 3570. Part D gains the CMDTIMEOUT step on both forms
''               (S-8's opt-in command timeout: a refreshed drive keeps running, an unrefreshed one stops and
''               is reported) and cells R17-DUAL-CMDTMO-D / R17-DUAL-WCMDTMO-D. STOPLIM now judges BOTH
''               wheels at their own limit, since driveForDistance() stops each wheel at its own distance
''               (finding AB). BM-DSTEP gains a step token and the cell set grows, so FMT goes to 6.
''               Task 3571 (PL-90/PL-69), same revision: each CLOCK lifetime prints BM-HALLINT (entries into
''               %000 and %111, and missed transitions) and folds R17-DUAL-HALL-K200 / -K270 / -K300.
''               Task 3572 (fault handling), same revision: the fault provocation is COMPUTED at speed per
