''               missed the test (PL-86, PL-59). BM-FLTAPI replaces want_off with l_shift / r_shift and appends
''               l_cause / r_cause (S-7). New cells R17-DUAL-FLTCAUSE-B, R17-DUAL-OFFREST-B, R17-DUAL-FLTSTOP-C
''               (a fault delivers holdAtStop(): FLOAT coasts further than BRAKE) and R17-DUAL-IDLEMOVE-A/-B/-C
''               (the uncommanded wheel stays put during the other wheel's trial)
''               18 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=16, FMT 7: task 3573 (PL-87, PL-78). Every LADDER and CLOCK rung
''               prints BM-RUNGTR, its TRANSITION from a mark at the command to the window start: peak |err|,
''               peak |i|, and tr_over (the transition peak above the rung's own steady err_pk). BM-RUNG2's
''               err_pk is the steady window's servo ripple and no longer read as a kick. New cell
''               R17-DUAL-TRKICK-A: a change of speed from a running speed kicks when its tr_over exceeds the
''               start from rest's by more than TRKICK_MARGIN.
''               18 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=17: task 3517, style-guide conformance, no record changes.
''               fltApiRetry() drops its unused trace id; US_PER_SEC and HALL_PIN_SPAN are the library's
