''               19 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=20, FMT 8: task 3577, bench cells for task 3569's promises. Part B's
''               OVERSHT gains two TURN trials, driveForDistance(10, 2) and (2, 10) ft, judged by the new cell
''               R17-DUAL-TURNDIST-B (each wheel at rest at its OWN limit) and printed as the new BM-TURN; for a
''               turn BM-OVERSHOOT's dist_ft and tgt print NA. STOPLIM is judged in the platform frame: the
''               steering object reverses the right wheel, so its raw rest is negative for forward travel
''               (Visit 5 read r_rest -529), and task 3570's per-wheel check compared that raw value against a
''               positive target -- a correct stop read 1_058 ticks off. Part D gains the step DIRSIGN and cell
''               R17-DUAL-DIRSIGN-D: a positive driveDirection() makes the RIGHT wheel the slower, a negative one
''               the LEFT (finding AC, judged wheels-lifted from the tracked ticks). The dead steerSetRamp() and
''               steerRestoreRamp() are deleted: since task 3569 setAcceleration() takes mm/s^2, not ramp_inc.
''               20 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=21, FMT 9: task 3580 (R18.1, PL-95, PL-87), the harness half. The
''               observables this harness reads were topping out exactly where the drive stops keeping up,
''               so above mid-range it was measuring a ceiling rather than the drive.
''               New record BM-RUNGHL, per measured rung: the driver's two UNBOUNDED health counters
''               (testGetDriveHealth()) differenced across the TRANSITION and across the STEADY window,
''               beside the field increment they convert by. err and duty stay in BM-RUNG2 unchanged, for
''               continuity with Visits 5 and 6a.
''               BM-RUNGTR gains from_incre (the speed the wheel was holding, so a transition's DELTA and
''               its DIRECTION are read off the record) and tr_i_over (the transition current peak above
''               the rung's own steady peak). R17-DUAL-TRKICK-A is re-judged on tr_i_over: tr_over is
''               err-derived and read 0 of 22 at Visit 6a while the transition current rose 75-fold
''               (PL-87's table), so the cell passed a kick Stephen felt with his hands.
''               LIVE now emits BM-RUNGTR and BM-RUNGHL for its rungs -- the short ramps, where he felt a
''               kick between rungs 2 and 3, had no transition record at all.
''               LADDER walks the ascent, then the DESCENT, then six delta cells: a small and a large
''               change of speed at low, at the saturation knee and at the ceiling, each taken up and
''               down. Visit 6a measured 44 speed-ups and zero speed-downs, and the same 20x10^6 step
''               taken at six places in the range spread six-fold, so WHERE a change happens dominates
''               HOW BIG it is.
''               21 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=22, FMT 10: task 3581 (R18.2 item 5), the LOW-SPEED regime, which
''               no test has ever covered and which is where BOTH position sources fail at once -- the
''               halls stop producing edges often enough to inform, and back-EMF is too small for the
''               phase voltages to carry angle.
''               New segment LOWSPD (part A, after LADDER): per motor x sign, one lifetime over lowIncre
''               (1..5 x 10^6). It is its own segment rather than four more ladder rungs because every
''               timing constant differs, and mixing two populations under one segment token would put
''               them in one verdict later.
''               rungMeasure() and rungWindow() take the window length as a parameter. LOWSPD needs
''               LOW_WINDOW_MS (4_000): at 1x10^6 the wheel turns 2.67 hall edges a second, so the
''               1_000 ms window every other rung uses would hold 2-3 ticks and any rate read from it is
''               quantisation rather than a measurement. Every existing caller passes WINDOW_MS, so no
''               measured rung changes.
''               New record BM-LOW: command-to-first-edge (does it start, and how long does starting
''               take) and the shortest and longest interval between hall edges across the window. The
''               sampling problem INVERTS down here -- at the top rung the instrument gets 1.1 samples
''               per hall edge and is blind between edges, at 1x10^6 it gets about 187 -- so the SHAPE
''               of the rotor's advance is visible here and nowhere else, and a spread between the two
''               gaps is cogging. No cell judges it: it is characterisation for R18.3, which picks the
''               acceptance numbers before R18.4 builds against them.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=24, FMT 12: task 3594, the ALIGN instrument's two defects (PL-99,
''               PL-100). The crossing detector gains a per-phase hysteresis band sized from the bias read's
''               own noise, and times each crossing at the midpoint of its raw sign flips so the band adds
''               no speed-dependent delay. The clip cell judges whether each phase's crossing BAND reaches a
''               rail, not whether its peaks do. BM-AGUIDE gains hyst_u/v/w_mV and band_railed; BM-ALEG's
''               clip becomes rail_pm (peak railing per thousand readings, no longer a saturated count) and
''               gains band_railed; BM-ACROSS t_us may now be negative (the crossing precedes its sector's
''               edge). Only the ALIGN part's records change.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=25, FMT 13: task 3600. BM-BUILD gains servo_engage, the DRIVER's
''               start seed (isp_bldc_motor SERVO_ENGAGE). The banner carried no driver identity at all, so
''               a log could not show whether a driver change was in the image; a driver without the seed
''               has no such constant, so the field's presence is the check.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=26, FMT 14: task 3594. BM-BUILD's servo_engage becomes drv_rev, the
''               driver's own hand-bumped DRIVER_REV. The start seed servo_engage marked was measured at Visit
''               7c pass 2 and removed, which left the field a constant that does not move when the driver
''               does -- the gap it was added to close, open again. drv_rev closes it for every driver change.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=27, FMT 15: task 3583 (R18.4). New part LEAD (-D DUAL_PART_LEAD, tier
''               dual-lead): at the driver's four lead-table speeds, per motor x sign, the commutation pair is
''               stepped LIVE through Z +- L for L = 18, 13, 8, 3, 23, 28, 33, each step an ordinary measured
''               rung; each speed ends with the new BM-LEADMIN (lead of least net current, bracketed or not),
''               and two new cells judge coverage and the quarter's known answer. The lead schedule is turned
''               back on at the end of every lifetime. Every other part's records are unchanged; drv_rev reads 2.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=28, FMT 16: task 3584 (Visit 8). Part A gains the TAKE segment and
''               BM-TAKE: A-6 (a slower command taken while SPIN_UP, R18-DUAL-TAKE-A) and A-8's following case
''               (R18-DUAL-FOLAGREE-A). Part D's BLOCKED step polls each wheel's path-limiter view through the
''               stall: A-7 (R18-DUAL-HOLDSET-D) and A-8's not-following case (R18-DUAL-NOTFOL-D). drv_rev reads 3.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=29, FMT 17: task 3601, from the Visit 8 evaluation. LEAD steps down to
''               -7 deg (nine steps: 18, 13, 8, 3, -2, -7, 23, 28, 33), since the quarter's minimum sat at the old
''               lowest step; R18-DUAL-LEAD-KNOWN is retired (its answer was the old servo's). Part D's A-8
''               not-following cell judges only a poll where the wheel IS short, and the new BM-HOLD logs what
''               both BLOCKED-step cells were judged on. drv_rev reads 4 (the lead table filled).
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=30, FMT 17: task 3601. R18-DUAL-OFFSETS-A expects the pair the lead
''               schedule gives at the wheel's present speed (testGetLead()), not the compiled fixed pair, which
''               is now the expectation only when the schedule is off. On the filled table it would otherwise
''               have failed every rung whose lead is not 18.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=31, FMT 17: task 3601, Visit 8b F-10. A LEAD step counts toward its
''               speed's minimum only if the wheel ran at >= LEAD_FOLLOW_PCT of its commanded rate: at too low a
''               lead the rotor slows, and a slower wheel draws less current for that reason alone.
''               22 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=32, FMT 18: task 3604 (DOCs/plans/LIMITS-RESET-PLAN.md E1-E4). New part
''               LIMITS (-D DUAL_PART_LIMITS; tiers dual-limits and, with -D DUTY_MAX_SVM, dual-limits-svm): LIMTOP
''               climbs to the unloaded top speed and prints BM-TOPSPD per motor x sign, with BM-CLIP per rung --
''               the PWM levels' range against the rails, from the instrument's new per-capture fold of the
''               driver's drive_u/v/w; LIMRAMP traces the start at ramp_inc 22/44/88 and a speed-down at
''               ramp_down 50k/100k (new cause SLOWER), each with BM-RAMP; LIMLOW measures four rungs from the
''               old floor down, then again with duty_min halved. The SVM build runs LIMTOP only. New cells
''               R18-DUAL-TOPSPD-M, R18-DUAL-PWMCLIP-M (and BM-CLIPTEST, the judge's own negative case),
''               R14-DUAL-TRACES-M. rungMeasure() takes the instrument's decimation. tokFinds and the plan
''               estimates gain the rows LEAD and TAKE were missing (PL-97's mechanism, third instance), and part
''               A now prints its LOWSPD and TAKE plan rows. drv_rev reads 6.
''               23 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=33, FMT 19: task 3605, from Visit 9. The duty ceiling it certified is the
''               drive's (drv_rev 7), so -D DUTY_MAX_SVM and tier dual-limits-svm are gone; -D LIMITS_TOP_ONLY (tier
''               dual-limits-top) builds the climb alone, the load that confirms moved limits. Each climb now ends
''               with the power check: driveAtPower(+-100) and (+-1) through the public API, read back against
''               the moved table as BM-POWER, judged by the new cell R18-DUAL-POWERMAP-M. DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE stays
''               147_000_000 as this harness's speed reference; the library's map is LIB_MAX/MIN_FWD_INCRE.
''               Same revision, task 3597: the certification of the driver's own following reading moves here from
''               the scan (R18-SCAN-FOLLOW retired, PL-98 (3)). Every clean LIMTOP rung and an over-command step
''               after each climb -- LIMTOP_MAX_INCRE under current limits lowered to OVERCMD_LIMIT_A, restored after
''               (BM-OCLIM) -- print BM-FOLLOW, and the new cells R18-DUAL-FOLLOW-M / R18-DUAL-FOLFALL-M judge the
''               driver against the harness on the populations the harness picks.
''               23 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=34, FMT 20: task 3613 (R19.7, Visit 10). New part FAULTRESP
''               (-D DUAL_PART_FAULTRESP, tier dual-fault): the fault study's X-cells (FAULT-STRATA-STUDY-2026-09-23.md
''               sec 7), on DRIVER_REV 12. Every fault is FORCED (testForceFault()), never provoked by an offset
''               shift (PL-119), and guarded: one that does not latch within FR_PROVOKE_MS stops the wheel and is
''               counted as the hook failing. FLTRESP, per wheel: the hook's own negative control first (a forced
''               fault at rest must not fault); at three ladder speeds the shipped response with holdAtStop(TRUE)
''               (X-2, the phase short) and FALSE (X-3, the coast, its phases at rest as its negative control); at
''               the middle speed FR_GRADED once (X-4, the re-sync, now onto the correct offsets) and twice on the
''               ramp (X-6, the graded short at 10/25/50/100 %, with the same double fault coasting as its lower
''               bound and X-2 as its full-short bound). FLTPLAT faults one wheel of the steering object and watches
''               the other stop (X-5, PL-117). The startup study's B-4 prints NOT_BUILT. New records BM-FRBUILD,
''               BM-NOTBUILT, BM-FRHOOK, BM-FRTRIAL, BM-FRSTAT, BM-FRCUR, BM-FRWIND, BM-FRPHASE, BM-FRREST, BM-FRPLAT;
''               BM-ABORT gains reason NO_FAULT; two why tokens. Every other part's records are unchanged
''               23 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=35, FMT 21: task 3613 (R19.7, Visit 10). New part START (-D DUAL_PART_START,
''               tier dual-start; with -D START_NO_WALK, tier dual-start-nowalk): the startup study's B-cells
''               (STARTUP-SELFTEST-STUDY-2026-09-23.md sec 6) through the steering object, on DRIVER_REV 12. SKCHECK
''               starts and stops the steering object SK_LIVES times, one lifetime each, and reads what start() judged:
''               getHealth(), the illegal hall codes, getPackVoltage() (PACK_NOT_FITTED on the bench) and every
''               BR_PROBE reading; then, in the same lifetime, a floated window through the instrument gives the
''               rest zero (as lifetimeZero() takes it: the driver's own restZeroSenseMv has no getter) and the three
''               phases' coast floor -- the probe's able-to-report control. The last SK_WALKS lifetimes also call
''               checkWiring() and rebuild each wheel's two legs from the ring. No PREFLT: the attended negatives
''               (B-1 halls unplugged, B-3 a lead unplugged, B-5 a hall pair swapped) load this same part, and a
''               preflight would drive the mis-wired wheel before a single start was read. New records BM-SKBUILD,
''               BM-SKHEALTH, BM-SKPROBE, BM-SKWALK, BM-SKSUM; the NOT_BUILT walk of the no-walk build reuses
''               BM-NOTBUILT. Every other part's records are unchanged
''               23 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=36, FMT 22: task 3591 (R18.2c tail, R19.8). New part SPIN (-D DUAL_PART_SPIN,
''               tier dual-spin): the spin-in-place FLOOR tier, loaded and attended -- the release's only
''               loaded measurement. SPIN runs twelve legs through the steering object, each armed with its own
''               distance stop at one revolution of the platform (derived from the 387 mm track width) before it is
''               driven, each clockwise leg followed by a counter-clockwise one: the confirmed offsets (the lead
''               schedule) at three speeds, the legacy pair as the control, the fixed pair at the quarter, and two
''               legs that fault one wheel on purpose. CREEP parks the loaded platform on a measured incline: a coast
''               control that must roll, a low-ceiling control that must slip, then the provisional hold ceiling.
''               The panel gains the DONE button and the SPIN / CREEP screens (tools/gen_dual_assets.py). New records
''               BM-SPINBUILD, BM-SPINPRE, BM-SPINLEG, BM-SPIN, BM-SPINW, BM-SPINSTART, BM-CRPBUILD, BM-CREEP, BM-CREEPW;
''               new cause SPIN, prompts SPIN and CREEP, operator events LETGO and CAUGHT, and four why tokens. Every
''               other part's records are unchanged; tokButton gains DONE at index 3, which BM-UISTEP prints by name
''               23 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=37, FMT 23: task 3614 (Visit 10 pass 2). The START part's negatives are made in
''               FIRMWARE, not by rewiring: the rig can unplug a wheel's hall connector but not a motor lead, and cannot
''               swap two hall wires (STEPHEN 2026-09-23). Both target the LEFT wheel, the board known to drive; the RIGHT
''               is the in-run control. -D START_NEG_PHASE (tier dual-start-phaseneg, no walk, as START_NO_WALK) withholds
''               one LEFT phase from every start's lead check (testLeftSetProbeWithhold()), U V W in turn, and the new cell
''               R19-DUAL-PHNEG-X counts the starts whose LEFT failed mask is not EXACTLY that phase's HLT_PHASE_* bit (a
''               dead bridge fails all three, so "some bit failed" could not tell one lead from the bridge). -D
''               START_NEG_SWAP (tier dual-start-swapneg) reads the LEFT wheel's hall bits 0 and 1 as swapped on every
''               walk lifetime (testLeftSetHallSwap(HSW_HALLS_01)), and the new cell R19-DUAL-SWNEG-X counts the walks in
''               which its HLT_WIRING was not judged failed. New record BM-SKNEG, printed before each armed start's
''               BM-SSTART; BM-SKBUILD appends neg (NONE / PHASE / SWAP) in every START build. No other record changes
''               24 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=38, FMT 24: task 3615 (PL-120, Visit 10 pass 2). New records BM-ABIL, BM-ABIS1..3
''               and BM-ABIP1..3: each driver's shared hub runs dumped RAW in isp_bldc_motor VAR order under the VAR's own
''               names -- the 4 launch longs, the status run and fault, the parameter run, and motorCog -- copied in one
''               pass before anything is printed. Where: SKSTART (part START, every lifetime whose steering start returned
