''               RE-CUT BY CONSTRUCTION, A-1 and A-2 (R19-DUAL-SPINSTRT-P, -SPINPEAK-P; spStartStats(), the SPIN CON
''               states each term): the jerk-limited ramp-out broke both instruments. A-2's reference was the 60 ms
''               before the first AT_SPEED, the ramp-out, still accelerating; it is now 60 ms of steady running,
''               A2_REF_DELAY_MS (420) after the first AT_SPEED -- where the servo model that set 1.8 took its own --
''               counted only when every sample to its end reads AT_SPEED, the driver's report that its acceleration is
''               0. A-1's window ends A1_RAMPOUT_SAMPLES (RAMP_TAU_MS + one sample) before the first AT_SPEED, so it
''               judges the rise, where the acceleration never falls, as the model's did. Both bounds (0.10, 1.8) are
