''               why for a settle the stop cut is the new token STOP_BEGAN (WHY_COUNT 47) where it said STEADY_TIMEOUT. H5: in
''               part SPIN the lag bound (R16-DUAL-LAGBND-P) starts when a wheel leaves STOPPED, not at the capture's arm, so
''               the pre-roll's resting rotor error (-111) is not read as lag. H6: SPINPEAK's criterion token is
''               START_I_OVR_STDY (the 24-character one printed ?). H7: sayCountdown() and sayResult() put a literal between
''               the formatted items DEBUG would otherwise separate with ", ". Every cell keeps its criterion and its negative
''               SRC_REV 70, FMT 45 (same revision, not yet shipped): THE TWO FLOOR SESSIONS (Plan A sec 10; Stephen 2026-09-30, R15
''               "As long as you don't need me interceding, running multiple checks per command is just fine", R16 the FlySky ramp
''               ranges, R17 "As long as you keep the robot in a 2 m by 2 m square area, it can run independently"). Part SPIN gains two
''               more actions beside the fourteen, each chaining checks with no operator step between them: -D FLOOR_ACT_AUTO (tier
''               floor-auto, SESSION 2: (1) the ten spin legs back to back in the leg table's order, RIGHT then LEFT at each of five
''               settings, each in its own pair lifetime with the driver's event log drained after it -- BM-EV stage SPIN, which the
''               spin logs never had -- so SPINSYM, SPINCTL and SPINLEAD are judged in one log; (2) the fault run, whole, as the single
''               action runs it, its two STAND CLEAR waits kept; (3) the RAMP LEGS: four straight 1 m legs, out and back twice, in one
''               lifetime at MEDIUM's power 13 (308 mm/s), at setAcceleration() / setDeceleration() of 200 / 1_000, 1_000 / 1_470,
''               3_000 / 3_000 and 1_000 / 1_470 mm/s^2 (the ends and middle of the FlySky knobs' ranges), the built-in rates restored
''               before the lifetime stops; the power is derived at RAMP_POWER (the rise at 200 plus the stop at 1_000 take 360 mm,
''               under half the leg), and each leg records the peak speed-up and slow-down the drivers' own drv_accel_now reported
''               (a hub read in spinWatch(), no library call), the time to AT_SPEED and the stop's travel, each beside the S-curve's
''               prediction -- no cell judges them) and -D FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE (tier floor-obstacle, SESSION 3: the COAST trial and
''               an ARMED drive back to its start by the travel the trial made, measured and at most 1 m; then the BRAKE trial and back;
''               a trial that ends in a fault drives back only when the platform is known clear -- both wheels at rest, the fault
''               recovered, no latch -- else the session ends and says so). THE FENCE (DBG_FENCE, these two images only): the
''               platform's position in the start frame is dead-reckoned from both wheels' hall counts (the instrument's mirror of
