''               02 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=76, FMT 51: task 3656 item 1 (PL-168, PL-132), after Stephen ruled D-5 in (2026-10-02).
''               THE BLOCKED STOP IS TIMED FROM THE DRIVER'S OWN COUNT. blockWatch() mirrors bFrontProtect()'s rule from each
''               driver's status run (a pass with no tick whose |err| >= LAG_SOFT or on which a limiter has acted since the wheel's
''               last tick, PL-179 F-a as SRC_REV 77 mirrors it; a tick, a state other than SPIN_UP / AT_SPEED for the limiter
''               half, or a pass with neither restarts it), and a latch must land BLOCKED_PASSES after the count began (BLK_COUNT_LO_MS ..
''               BLK_COUNT_HI_MS, 988-1,012 ms); NO_LATCH fires when a count has run BLK_NOLATCH_MS (1,024). The old upper bound,
''               timed from the last tick (1,168, with a 156 ms field-travel allowance) gave up on the 2026-09-30 rocking stand
''               before the driver's count could finish; it and blkTickAfterAt are deleted. BLKSTOP and BLKLIMIT judge the same
''               bounds. BM-BLOCK gains l_count and r_count (257 bytes worst case); BM-BLKBUILD's lag_ms and stand_hi become
''               count_lo and count_hi. With D-5 the COAST trial against a yielding stand is expected to latch.
''               02 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=77, FMT 52: PL-179 and PL-180 (task 3662, DRIVER_REV 48), the harness half. THE MIRROR FOLLOWS F-a:
''               blockWatch()'s limiter half is now sticky, as bFrontProtect()'s bLimSinceTick is -- a per-wheel flag (blkLimTick) set by
''               the first pass with no tick on which duty_capped + foldback_frames moved in SPIN_UP / AT_SPEED, cleared by a tick or by
''               a state other than those two, and read by the count (the 2026-10-02 stall acted in single frames, so the old per-pass
''               test restarted the mirrored count at every quiet pass and the driver's count, which now does not, ran on). The count
''               also takes the driver's state test (SPIN_UP, AT_SPEED or SPIN_DN). BLK_COUNT_LO_MS / BLK_COUNT_HI_MS stand. Two new
''               cells, both on the OBSTACLE trials (floor-obstacle-coast, floor-obstacle-short, floor-obstacle): R22-DUAL-BLKWIN-P
''               (I-9: after a stalled wheel's first limiter action and while it has no tick, its |err| never reads 82..88, the band
''               one hall tick against the field faults from; read from the status run on every blockWatch() pass) and
''               R22-DUAL-BLKFLT-P (the trial latches with no EV_FAULT and no EV_FAULT_RESYNC on either wheel, read from the event
''               drain). Each prints NOMEAS with a why on the new record BM-BLKWIN (FMT 52; 218 bytes worst case), one per trial,
''               after the trial's BM-SR; two new whys, NO_LIMITER_ACTION and EVENTS_LOST (WHY_COUNT 55). Every existing cell is kept.
''               BLKSTOP now also judges a trial that met the obstacle at AT_SPEED and neither latched nor stood BLK_NOLATCH_MS
''               (the harness's timeout, or an abort on a fault) as a FAIL: the 2026-10-02 COAST trial, its own negative, read NOMEAS.
''               02 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=78 (no format change): PL-182, PL-183, PL-185 and the traced slow leg (task 3664), the floor
''               tests the 2026-10-02 visit disproved. PL-182: LIMGIVE limb (a) counts a give-way slot only after the wheel's driver
''               read DCS_AT_SPEED on the leg (limSample(), bLgArrived, LG_STATE_IDX); a held pass in SPIN_UP is the ramp not yet there.
''               The held count (BM-LIMW held, SPINHOLD) is unchanged. PL-183: A-2 (SPINPEAK) reads the ARRIVAL, the peak over
''               A2_ARR_SAMPLES samples from the first AT_SPEED sample, not the whole spin-up's acceleration plateau, and is judged as
''               that peak's excess over the steady mean in mV against TRKICK's 50 (A2_EXCESS_MV_HI; criterion ARRIVE_I_OVER_MV, units
''               MV), not as a ratio: at a 12-19 mV floor tail one count is 5-8 %. BM-SPINSTART's pk_i is that window's peak and its
''               ratio_x100 still prints (the record's shape is the same). PL-185: LOAD_LIMIT_A 4 -> 2 (and
''               gen_dual_assets.py's: its panel bitmap reads 4 until regenerated). Spin leg 2 (SLOW, SCHED, LEFT) drains its capture as a
''               trace (bSpLegTraced(), BM-SPIN traced), with no START cell; FLOOR_EST_KB 450 -> 575, FLOOR_EST_S 182, the cap 550.
''               02 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=79 (no format change; INSTRUMENTATION, no new verdict cell -- the cells come once the study says what
''               the trace must show): PL-187 (task 3668), the rough running above 175 x 10^6. Part LIMITS' LIMTOP traces, per wheel and
''               direction, the climb's EDGE rung (its first not-clean rung: 185 x 10^6, STEADY_TIMEOUT, on 2026-10-02) and the
''               OVER-COMMAND step (LIMTOP_MAX_INCRE at OVERCMD_LIMIT_A): each a BM-TRACE, BM-TS lines and a BM-TRACE-END, seg LIMTOP, cause
''               EDGE or OVERCMD (two new values of BM-TRACE's cause token; the table walk of R21-DUAL-TOKTAB reads them). BM-TS already
''               carries what the study needs per sample -- e (err), d (duty), i, ph, u, v, w, pos, hw, st -- and is unchanged (308 bytes
''               worst case); the PWM levels are not per sample (the ring's sample is full), BM-CLIP's room stays the capture's least.
''               limTrace() drains the capture rungMeasure() took (decimation 1, 2 ms) just after the edge is found, before the recovery
''               re-arms the ring, and the over-command step now arms the instrument before its command and freezes it as its window
''               closes (before, it ran unarmed): 3_010 samples for a rung that times out, about 2_030 for the step, against a ring of
''               4_096 (8.19 s). The log carries up to TRACE_EMIT_MAX = 400 lines a trace, so the first 100 samples and the last
''               LIMTRACE_TAIL_SAMPLES (100) are every 2 ms and the middle is strided (16 samples, 32 ms, at these lengths). bTraceDrain() takes
''               four one-shot shapes, all zero for every other trace: bTrWhole (the ring's event mark is ignored, so a rung's window
''               marks cannot trim its approach; BM-TRACE-END's mark_k reads NA and why NOT_REACHED), trTail, trStrideCap (the fit may
''               grow the stride to 32) and trWatch (the wheel is still driven while the drain runs, so traceWatchPoll() reads its
''               safety every SAMPLE_MS inside the walks; an absolute-current abort stops it as in any watched wait). The over-command
''               trace drains BEFORE the current limits are put back, so the wheel is held at OVERCMD_LIMIT_A throughout. The study traces
''               are not counted into R14-DUAL-TRACES-M. LIMTOP's plan row: 360 s and 90 KB -> 380 s and 1_080 KB (BM-TRACE 233 and
''               BM-TRACE-END 277 bytes, both unchanged; no record grows). No debug() statement is added: the footprint is unchanged.
''               03 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=80 (no format change): from the second 6.1.0 visit (VISIT-6.1.0B-EVALUATION.md). PL-188: the
''               obstacle mirror kept its count on the pass that first sees a wheel in DCS_ESTOP -- that is the latch, which this pass
''               sees before its latch check; the SRC_REV 77 state test zeroed it there, so BLKSTOP and BLKLIMIT read a count of 0 on
''               two correct latches (stands 1_022 and 1_002 ms). PL-182: the slow spin leg's trace emits every sample (trEmitMax, a
''               fifth one-shot shape of bTraceDrain(); 1_711 lines on 2026-10-02, where 394 could not place its held passes);
''               floor-auto's plan grows to about 980 KB and 185 s, its cap to 560 s.
''               03 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=81, FMT 53: PL-189, PL-187 (task 3668, HOLD-SPEED-UNDER-LOAD-DESIGN.md sec 4.12.8): THE CERTIFICATION
''               OF DRIVER_REV 49's HOLD (T-1 + U-1 + U-2 + U-5), each cell able to fail on the second visit's logs (DOCs/analyses/bench/
''               2026-10-02b/). TWO NEW CELLS. R22-DUAL-LDFLT-P (floor-grab; I-9'): no EV_FAULT and no EV_FAULT_RESYNC on either wheel from the
''               grab point to the leg's end, judged only when the gripped wheel was slowed but moving (BM-LOADW l_pct LDFLT_PCT_LO 5 ..
''               LDFLT_PCT_HI 60), else NOMEAS with a why on the new record BM-LDFLT; its negative is debug_261002-143538.log (EV_FAULT_RESYNC
''               seq 16, EV_FAULT seq 19, l_pct 19). R22-DUAL-OVRSTEP-M (dual-limits; I-12): after each over-command the full-power step
''               completes -- its BM-POWER why NONE and no BM-ABORT in it (limPowerCheck()'s full-power window ends on no safety event); its
''               negative is debug_261002-142002.log (BM-ABORT seq 161 ABS_CURRENT, BM-POWER seq 162 ABORTED); a step not reached is NOMEAS,
''               and each step prints the new record BM-OVRSTEP. THREE CORRECTIONS. BLKWIN's flag reads foldback_frames alone (blkWinFold,
''               blkFoldPrev), as T-1 arms on the fold-back only; the blocked-count mirror keeps duty_capped + foldback_frames, which
''               bFrontProtect() still reads at DRIVER_REV 49. LDHOLD is judged only when the gripped wheel ran LDHOLD_PCT_LO (15) % or more
''               of its command (a steady hold near a stop gives 1_127-1_142 ms gaps on a correct drive: sec 4.12.8), else NOMEAS NEAR_STOP.
''               TWO PREMISE CHANGES (S-b, sec 4.12.7: while a wheel is held at its current limit drv_incr is not the field's speed): LDPATH is
''               NOMEAS LIMIT_HELD when the gripped wheel's fold-back engaged during the judged window (it still judges a hold that slowed the
''               wheel with no limit acting), and the over-command's BM-FOLLOW readings (kind OVER) print why FIELD_NOT_SPEED (their
''               drv_incr is not the field's speed) but still fold into FOLLOW / FOLFALL, which compare measured rpm windows. BM-LOAD's tokens, LDPATH's and LDHUNT's
''               criteria are otherwise unchanged. New records BM-LDFLT (GRAB, 192 bytes worst) and BM-OVRSTEP (LIMITS, 84); BM-FOLLOW appends
''               why (201); four why tokens (NEAR_STOP, NOT_SLOWED, LIMIT_HELD, FIELD_NOT_SPEED; WHY_COUNT 59). evDrain() also stamps each
''               log's EV_FAULT / EV_FAULT_RESYNC after evdFltSinceMs and the EV_FOLDBACK reading against the judged window. No debug()
''               statement is added: the footprint is unchanged.
''               03 Oct 2026 -- SRC_REV=82, FMT 53: PL-182, PL-192 (sprint closeout, HOLD-SPEED-SPRINT-PLAN.md): TWO HARNESS CORRECTIONS
''               from the third visit (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-10-02c/). PL-182: traceWalk() capped its emission at TRACE_EMIT_MAX
''               apart from trEmitMax, so the slow spin leg's full trace stopped at the usual cap; it now caps at TRACE_EMIT_MAX #>
''               trEmitMax. PL-192: LDHUNT counted a wheel's first path-limiter engage inside the window as a transition, so a hold
''               that engaged once and held to the stop (15_588 ms on 2026-10-02c) read 1 and failed; evDrain() now keeps that onset
''               apart (evdPathOn), and loadEngages() counts it toward the engaged precondition, not the flips. The hunting negative
''               (an engage and release every 720-790 ms) still reads well above 0. No record, token or footprint change.
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHAT THIS BINARY IS

  Governing design: DOCs/plans/MOTION-HARNESS-DESIGN.md, with its section 12 arbiter rulings.

  NO EXTERNAL MEASUREMENT (STEPHEN 2026-09-14). Every reading comes from the driver's own status
  block, its calibrated sense channel and the hall inputs.

  ONE SOURCE, ONE PART PER BUILD. tools/bench-run.sh chooses the part with -D DUAL_PART_A,
  DUAL_PART_CLOCK, DUAL_PART_B, DUAL_PART_BRAKE, DUAL_PART_C, DUAL_PART_D, DUAL_PART_FLOOR, DUAL_PART_UICHECK,
  DUAL_PART_ALIGN, DUAL_PART_LEAD, DUAL_PART_LIMITS, DUAL_PART_FAULTRESP, DUAL_PART_START, DUAL_PART_SPIN,
  DUAL_PART_PACK, DUAL_PART_REG or DUAL_PART_KICK. DUAL_PART_SPIN takes one more symbol (SRC_REV 69), the ONE floor action:
  FLOOR_ACT_OBST_COAST, _OBST_SHORT, _GRAB, _FAULTRUN or _SPIN_{SLOW,MED,FAST,LEGACY,FIXED}_{LEFT,RIGHT}; with none it runs
  nothing. SRC_REV 70: or one of two SESSIONS that chain checks with no operator step between them, inside a 2 m square from his
  fixed start point and back to it: FLOOR_ACT_AUTO (the ten spins, the fault run and the ramp legs) or FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE (the
  COAST and BRAKE trials, each with a drive back).
  PART_ID comes from one #ifdef chain; with no part flag the build prints part NONE, runs no segment, and ends cleanly.
  ONE PART PER IMAGE (PL-152, SRC_REV 54): the same chain defines a DBP_* symbol per part, and each part's code is
  compiled only into its own image (the build-variant CON says how); the shared plumbing is in every image.

  COG MODEL
   - cog 0: runs every command and every emitter; never calls a library getter inside a timed wait.
   - instrument cog: samples both motors every INST_PERIOD_TICKS into one ring on one timebase. Its
     call graph holds no debug() statement (I1), it holds no lock, and it stops cooperatively (I4).
   - watchdog cog: watches cog 0's heartbeat; on a stall it stops wheelL, wheelR and steering, then
     ends the session (test_bench_scan.spin2's pattern, extended).

  INVARIANTS named in the design's section 1 (I1-I12) are cited where the code keeps them.

  RECORDS: tag-first BM- records, one debug(zstr_()) line each through emitRecord(), run-wide seq
  as the second field, every field clamped, worst case under 280 bytes (stated at each emitter; BM-TS is 308 since SRC_REV 70,
  inside the 640-byte line buffer of isp_bench_log).

  HOW IT IS RUN (from the repo root; each load adds -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_QUIET and its part flag)

      tools/bench-run.sh dual-a | dual-clock-200 | dual-clock-270 | dual-clock-300 | dual-b | dual-brake
                         | dual-c | dual-d | dual-floor | dual-ui | dual-align | dual-lead | dual-limits
                         | dual-limits-top | dual-fault | dual-fault-rightfirst | dual-start | dual-start-nowalk
                         | dual-start-phaseneg | dual-start-swapneg | dual-pack | dual-reg | dual-kick
                         | dual-tokneg

      SRC_REV 71: dual-tokneg is no part (PART_NONE, nothing moves, seconds): -D TOKCHK_NEG removes one entry from one token
      table and makes one token too long, and the R21-DUAL-TOKTAB cell must print FAIL (the self-check's own negative)

      SRC_REV 69: part SPIN is fourteen tiers, one action each, none with a window or an input (each adds -D DUAL_PART_SPIN
      and its own -D FLOOR_ACT_*): floor-obstacle-coast | floor-obstacle-short | floor-grab | floor-faultrun
                         | floor-spin-{slow,med,fast,legacy,fixed}-{left,right}
      (the old dual-spin tier, the countdown-board run, is abandoned, R10)

      SRC_REV 70: and the two SESSIONS (-D DUAL_PART_SPIN with -D FLOOR_ACT_AUTO or -D FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE): floor-auto | floor-obstacle

  (the clock is part of the tier name, so a mistyped clock is an unknown tier and is refused -- PL-62)

  DEBUG RECORD BUDGET (design sec 6.2). Ceiling: 255 debug records per compiled program.

    source                                         records  how counted
    test_bench_dual.spin2, records and markers           5  read: main() DEBUG_END_SESSION,
                                                            emitRecord(), the panic line in
                                                            emitHeaderRecords(), declareStall()
                                                            DEBUG_END_SESSION, wdEmitRecord()
    test_bench_dual.spin2, operator panel               23  read, parts BRAKE, FLOOR and UICHECK only (SRC_REV 69:
                                                            not SPIN, which opens no window): panelSetup() 12
                                                            (PLOT, CARTESIAN, 8 x
                                                            LAYER, CROP 1, UPDATE); panelRender() 9 (prompt
                                                            CROP, state CROP, button CROP, button
                                                            restore CROP, digit CROP, countdown-label
                                                            CROP, strip CROP, heartbeat CROP, UPDATE);
                                                            panelReadInput() 2 (PC_KEY, PC_MOUSE)
    test_bench_dual.spin2, plain operator lines          4  read, part SPIN (SRC_REV 69; the countdown board's 20, part
                                                            SPIN only, are gone with it): alignSay() 1 (the lead-in's
                                                            stand line), sayCountdown() 1 (the lead-in's timed line and
                                                            FAULTRUN's two STAND CLEAR lines), sayResult() 2 (the
                                                            RESULT line, with and without a cause: SRC_REV 70).
                                                            SRC_REV 70: the two SESSIONS (floor-auto, floor-obstacle,
                                                            the DBG_FENCE images) carry 6: sayFenceRefusal() 1 (a leg the
                                                            fence refused) and saySkipped() 1 (an action or the straight
                                                            actions skipped) more. The sessions' progress lines reuse
                                                            alignSay(); their RESULT line is composed in a buffer and
                                                            printed by sayResult(): no new statement.
                                                            ALIGN and PACK carry alignSay() 1 alone
    isp_bench_log.spin2                                  0  read: no debug statement
    isp_bldc_motor.spin2 under the quiet masks          20  DEBUG-CHANNELS-DESIGN.md: ERROR 17 +
                                                            WARNING 3
    isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 under the quiet masks     10  DEBUG-CHANNELS-DESIGN.md: ERROR 10
    TOTAL, each object image counted once               39  of 255 for each single-action SPIN image (5 + 4 + 30), 41 for each
                                                            of the two sessions (5 + 6 + 30); 58 in the parts with the
                                                            panel (BRAKE, FLOOR, UICHECK), 36 in ALIGN and PACK, 35 in the rest
    TOTAL, each of the four motor instances counted     99  of 255 for each single-action SPIN image, 101 for each session;
                                                            118, 96 and 95 in those other parts
                                                            (wheelL, wheelR and the steering object's two, design sec 11 fact 9)

  The library rows hold only under -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_QUIET. The builds tools/build-check.sh makes
  without those flags enable more library channels; there, as for every build, the compiler accepting
  the program is the confirmation that the ceiling holds, and this table is the count, not a measurement.

  PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY.
}

' Select the two-wheel configuration in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (a -D BENCH_CFG build uses the bench file instead)
#DEFINE CFG_DUAL_MOTOR
#IFDEF __PNUT_TS__
#PRAGMA EXPORTDEF CFG_DUAL_MOTOR
#ENDIF

' SRC_REV 71: -D TOKCHK_NEG (tier dual-tokneg) is the token self-check's own negative case: it is both of its limbs, and each
'  limb is also a flag of its own so a desk compile can show each alone flip the cell. TOKCHK_NEG_SHORT removes one token from
'  the scope table (tokScope); TOKCHK_NEG_LONG lengthens one token of the exit table (tokExit) past its field. Every other
'  build compiles the tables as they are.
#ifdef TOKCHK_NEG
#define TOKCHK_NEG_SHORT
#define TOKCHK_NEG_LONG
#endif

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 82                              ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 53                                   ' BM- record-format version
    SF_VERSION  = 1                                         ' sign-off format (VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B.1)

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' the one clock line bench-run.sh patches
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    MS_PER_SEC = wheelL.MS_PER_SEC
    US_PER_SEC = wheelL.US_PER_SEC
    TICKS_PER_MS = CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC
    TICKS_PER_US = CLK_FREQ / US_PER_SEC

    ' p2kbSpin2Waitms: a waitms() argument must stay at or under $8000_0000 clocks. Unsigned divide,
    '  since $8000_0000 is negative as a signed long. 7_953 ms at 270 MHz, 7_158 at 300, 10_737 at 200.
    WAITMS_MAX_MS = $8000_0000 +/ (CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC)

    ' every waitms() argument in this file is one of these five, each far under WAITMS_MAX_MS
    SAMPLE_MS         = 5                                   ' cog-0 poll cadence of every beat-polled loop
    OPER_POLL_MS      = 50                                  ' operator loops, under PC_KEY's ~100 ms latch
    INST_EXIT_POLL_MS = 50                                  ' the instrument's parked loop after EXIT
    WD_POLL_MS        = 250                                 ' watchdog sample cadence
    WD_IDLE_MS        = 1_000                               ' idle-forever chunk

CON { build variant -- the part, from one #ifdef chain, never a runtime test }

  ' Part built into this image (design sec 4.1):
  '  PART_NONE  - no part flag: no segment runs
  '  PART_A     - PREFLT, STOPMODE, LIVE, LADDER
  '  PART_CLOCK - PREFLT, CLOCK (built three times, at 200/270/300 MHz)
  '  PART_B     - PREFLT, FAULTB, OVERSHT
  '  PART_BRAKE - OUTSIDE (attended: one hand-brake)
  '  PART_C     - PREFLT, BASELINE, POSTFLT
  '  PART_D     - PREFLT, STEERSEG, LIMIT (task 3560: the front cog's contract and current limiting)
  '  PART_FLOOR - FLOOR (attended: wheels down, brief observation)
  '  PART_UICHECK - UICHECK (attended: every panel control and attended screen, no motor control at all)
  '  PART_ALIGN - ALIGN (attended: the wheel is turned BY HAND against a coasting bridge; task 3590)
  '  PART_LEAD  - PREFLT, LEAD (the live lead-step run that measures the dynamic-lead table; task 3583)
  '  PART_LIMITS - PREFLT, LIMTOP, LIMRAMP, LIMLOW (the limits reset's experiments E1-E4; task 3604); the
  '               LIMITS_TOP_ONLY build runs PREFLT and LIMTOP only
  '  PART_FAULTRESP - PREFLT, FLTRESP, FLTPLAT (the fault study's X-cells, faults forced at speed; task 3613); the
  '               FRESP_RIGHT_FIRST build runs the RIGHT wheel's own FLTRESP trials before the LEFT's (PL-120)
  '  PART_START - SKCHECK (the startup study's B-cells through the steering object, no PREFLT; task 3613); the
  '               START_NO_WALK and START_NEG_PHASE builds never call checkWiring(); START_NEG_PHASE and START_NEG_SWAP
  '               arm a firmware negative on the LEFT wheel (task 3614); START and START_NEG_PHASE arm the winding
  '               check (task 3610, BUILD_WIND)
  '  PART_SPIN  - ONE floor action per image (SRC_REV 69, -D FLOOR_ACT_*): OBSTACLE's coast or short trial, GRAB, FAULTRUN,
  '               or one spin leg (attended, wheels down, no window: the floor run's situations under Stephen's
  '               floor rules -- the protective stop on an obstacle, one side held back, a fault on a drive back and the
  '               drive after it, the loaded spin-in-place legs; INCLINE is postponed and compiled out; no PREFLT, whose
  '               single-wheel nudge would pivot a platform on the floor; task 3591, SRC_REV 62). SRC_REV 70: or a SESSION, FLOOR_ACT_AUTO
  '               or FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE -- several of these actions chained with no operator step between them, inside a 2 m square
  '               from his fixed start point and back to it (the section "the floor sessions" below)
  '  PART_PACK  - PACK (attended, nothing moves: the pack voltage sensor read steady, unplugged and replugged twice at
  '               the pack, and its meter pairs; task 3611, R20.4). Built with user.PACK_SENSOR_FITTED FALSE it reads
  '               nothing and every pack cell prints NOT_BUILT
  '  PART_REG   - PREFLT, REGRESS (PL-151's part-B half, pointed: TURNDIST through the steering object, and a fault
  '               forced with testForceFault() on each wheel for FLTCAUSE and PL-66's FLTRETRY; wheels up, unattended)
  '  PART_KICK  - PREFLT, KICK (the speed-change kick at the top of the range, PL-78 / PL-87: seven transitions per
  '               wheel and direction through the ladder's own rung instrument; wheels up, unattended)
    #0, PART_NONE, PART_A, PART_CLOCK, PART_B, PART_BRAKE, PART_C, PART_D, PART_FLOOR, PART_UICHECK, ...
        PART_ALIGN, PART_LEAD, PART_LIMITS, PART_FAULTRESP, PART_START, PART_SPIN, PART_PACK, PART_REG, PART_KICK
    PART_COUNT = PART_KICK + 1

  ' The floor action built into a PART_SPIN image (SRC_REV 69, Stephen 2026-09-30, R4: "we just run the test sequentially.
  '  Again."): one action, chosen by one -D FLOOR_ACT_* symbol beside -D DUAL_PART_SPIN, and run once:
  '  FLA_NONE            - no symbol: nothing moves, BM-PLAN names no action, the RESULT line says none was selected
  '  FLA_OBST_COAST      - OBSTACLE's coast trial (the bridge coasts once the protective stop latches)
  '  FLA_OBST_SHORT      - OBSTACLE's brake trial, the control (the stop shorts the bridge)
  '  FLA_GRAB            - one GRAB trial
  '  FLA_FAULTRUN        - the fault return run, one sequence
  '  FLA_SPIN_<kind>_RIGHT / _LEFT - one spin leg, clockwise (RIGHT) or counter-clockwise (LEFT), of one of five kinds, each
  '                        a pair of the old ten-leg run: SLOW, MED (MEDIUM) and FAST (BRISK, the quarter) on the SCHED
  '                        offsets, then LEGACY (MEDIUM on the legacy pair, SPINCTL's control) and FIXED (the quarter on
  '                        the fixed pair, SPINLEAD's denominator). The order is load-bearing: (action - FLA_SPIN_SLOW_RIGHT)
  '                        / 2 indexes spinActPair and // 2 is SPIN_DIR_*
  '  FLA_AUTO            - SRC_REV 70, SESSION 2 of DOCs/plans/archive/WINDOW-FREE-BENCH-SPRINT-PLAN.md sec 10 (R15): the ten spin legs, the
  '                        fault run and the ramp legs, back to back, inside the 2 m square (R17)
  '  FLA_OBSTACLE        - SRC_REV 70, SESSION 3: the COAST trial, an armed drive back to the start, the BRAKE trial, and back
  '  FLA_PLAN_SPINS, FLA_PLAN_FAULT, FLA_PLAN_RAMP - BM-PLAN's action for FLOOR_ACT_AUTO's three parts (plan rows only; FLOOR_ACT is
  '                        never one of them). FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE's two rows name FLA_OBST_COAST and FLA_OBST_SHORT
    #0, FLA_NONE, FLA_OBST_COAST, FLA_OBST_SHORT, FLA_GRAB, FLA_FAULTRUN, FLA_SPIN_SLOW_RIGHT, FLA_SPIN_SLOW_LEFT, ...
        FLA_SPIN_MED_RIGHT, FLA_SPIN_MED_LEFT, FLA_SPIN_FAST_RIGHT, FLA_SPIN_FAST_LEFT, FLA_SPIN_LEGACY_RIGHT, ...
        FLA_SPIN_LEGACY_LEFT, FLA_SPIN_FIXED_RIGHT, FLA_SPIN_FIXED_LEFT, FLA_AUTO, FLA_OBSTACLE, FLA_PLAN_SPINS, ...
        FLA_PLAN_FAULT, FLA_PLAN_RAMP
    FLA_COUNT = FLA_PLAN_RAMP + 1

  ' ONE PART PER IMAGE (PL-152, SRC_REV 54). Each branch below also #defines its own DBP_* symbol, and every part's
  '  code -- its segments, its tables, its state and its emitters -- sits behind that symbol (or behind a DBG_* group
  '  symbol, defined after this chain, when two or more parts share it), so a build compiles its own part and the
  '  shared plumbing only. Until SRC_REV 53 the part flag chose what RAN, not what COMPILED: every tier carried all
  '  fifteen parts (pass 6's images were all 152,139 B) and each compile took about 13 s. The DBP_* symbols come from
  '  this one chain, so they are exclusive and follow its precedence exactly as PART_ID does; nothing tests a
  '  DUAL_PART_* flag directly after it.
  ' RUN_TIME_CAP_S per load (design sec 4.2 item 6)
#ifdef DUAL_PART_A
#define DBP_A
    PART_ID        = PART_A
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_500
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_CLOCK
#define DBP_CLOCK
    PART_ID        = PART_CLOCK
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 300
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_B
#define DBP_B
    PART_ID        = PART_B
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_200
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_BRAKE
#define DBP_BRAKE
    PART_ID        = PART_BRAKE
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 600
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_C
#define DBP_C
    PART_ID        = PART_C
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 900
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_D
#define DBP_D
    PART_ID        = PART_D
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 900
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_FLOOR
#define DBP_FLOOR
    PART_ID        = PART_FLOOR
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 600
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_UICHECK
#define DBP_UICHECK
    PART_ID        = PART_UICHECK
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_500
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_ALIGN
#define DBP_ALIGN
    PART_ID        = PART_ALIGN
    ' eight hand-turned legs, each waiting on a person and each bounded by ALIGN_STALL_MS rather than by
    '  a clock the operator cannot see: the cap has to cover eight full stalls and still end the run
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_800
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_LEAD
#define DBP_LEAD
    PART_ID        = PART_LEAD
    ' 2 motors x 2 signs x LEAD_RUNGS x LEAD_STEPS = 112 measured rungs of ~2-8 s, plus lifetimes
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_500
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_LIMITS
#define DBP_LIMITS
    PART_ID        = PART_LIMITS
    ' about 17.3 minutes planned (emitPlan()): LIMTOP ~6.3, LIMRAMP ~5, LIMLOW ~6
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_800
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_FAULTRESP
#define DBP_FAULTRESP
    PART_ID        = PART_FAULTRESP
    ' about 6 minutes planned (emitPlan()): 24 driven wheel trials of ~13 s, 2 at-rest hook checks of ~4 s and 2
    '  steering trials of ~15 s, each with its own lifetime and a FAULT_COOL_MS cool-down; the cap leaves room for
    '  every trial to take its restart. PL-120's recovery probe, which runs only after a no-motion failure and at most
    '  once, adds at most FR_RECOVER_TRIES x FR_RECOVER_GAP_MS (2 minutes) plus its last try's lifetime. PL-136: a wheel
    '  that does not move at PREFLT adds its PF_RETRY_TRIES retries (about 5 s each) and, if they all fail, a PREFLT
    '  probe of the same 2 minutes, before FLTRESP; the FLTRESP probe can still run once after that. Worst case about
    '  6 + 2.2 + 2.2 = 10.5 minutes, under the cap
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 900
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_START
#define DBP_START
    PART_ID        = PART_START
    ' about 60 s planned (emitPlan()): SK_LIVES steering lifetimes of ~3.5 s (spacing, the ~1.2 s start, the reads,
    '  a 1 s floated window) and SK_WALKS walks of ~1.5 s (PL-137: 10 in dual-start, was 3); the cap is three times
    '  that, well short of an idle hang
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 180
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_SPIN
#define DBP_SPIN
    PART_ID        = PART_SPIN
    ' SRC_REV 69: ONE ACTION PER IMAGE, chosen by one -D FLOOR_ACT_* symbol (the same chain as the part's: the first
    '  symbol given wins, so an image holds exactly one action). Each branch defines its DBF_* symbol, the code only that
    '  action runs sits behind it, and gives the action's plan: FLOOR_EST_S and FLOOR_EST_KB are BM-PLAN's est_s and
    '  est_kb, RUN_TIME_CAP_S its cap. NO SCREEN WAITS ON HIM NOW: every time below is the program's own, so each cap is
    '  derived from the run's bounded waits -- about three times the planned seconds, never an idle hang.
  ' SRC_REV 70: the two SESSIONS (R15: a command may chain many checks when none needs him in between), each compiled from the
  '  single actions' own code plus its session-only additions (DBF_AUTO, DBF_OBSTSESS, and the DBG_FENCE group they share):
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_AUTO
#define DBF_AUTO
#define DBF_SPINLEG
#define DBF_FAULTRUN
#define DBF_RAMP
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_AUTO
    ' SESSION 2, about 180 s planned (SRC_REV 74: was 170): LEAD_IN_MS 10 s, then three parts whose rows BM-PLAN prints. (1) The ten spin
    '  legs, AUTO_EST_SPIN_S 90 s (was 80): each leg its own lifetime (the ~1.3 s start, the turn, its records and the event drain
    '  EV_SETTLE_MS ~1 s, the close), from the first floor visit's own segment times -- SLOW 11.2 and 11.6 s, MEDIUM 6.1-6.5 s, the
    '  quarter 4.5-6.1 s (the traced legs the longer) -- plus the drain: 2 x (12.5 + 7.5 + 7.2 + 7.0 + 5.6) s = 79.6 s with the one-turn
    '  quarter. SRC_REV 74: the quarter's legs turn twice, 211 more ticks at 98.2 ticks a second = 2.2 s unloaded each, and each
    '  quarter window is 200 ms longer: 2 x (12.5 + 7.5 + 7.2 + 9.4 + 8.0) = 89.2 s, planned 90 s. (2) The fault run, AUTO_EST_FR_S 50 s: the one
    '  sequence of FLOOR_ACT_FAULTRUN without its lead-in (its est_s 65 less 10, a little under). (3) The ramp legs, AUTO_EST_RAMP_S
    '  30 s: one lifetime (~1.3 s), four legs of 1 m (3.8-4.4 s at power 13) each with its event drain (about 1 s), and the stop.
    '  About 575 KB (SRC_REV 78: was 450): the two traced quarter legs (about 110 KB each), the slow LEFT leg's trace (spin leg 2: it
    '  runs to the end of its 2_000 ms window, 0.4 s of spin-up + 1 s settle + 2 s + the pre-roll, about 3.7 s at the 110 KB / 3.1 s
    '  the quarter's traces cost, so about 125 KB), the fault run's trace (about 120 KB) and the records. The ring holds 8.19 s, so
    '  the slow leg's start is not overwritten. Its drain adds about 2 s. The cap is three times the plan, to whole tens of seconds.
    '  SRC_REV 80 (PL-182): the slow leg emits every sample (trEmitMax), not 400 lines: its 2026-10-02 trace stored 1_711 at 308
    '  bytes worst, about 530 KB in place of about 125, and about 3 s more to send at 2 Mbaud: about 980 KB, 185 s, the cap 560
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 185
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 980
    AUTO_EST_SPIN_S  = 95
    AUTO_EST_SPIN_KB = 810
    AUTO_EST_FR_S    = 50
    AUTO_EST_FR_KB   = 130
    AUTO_EST_RAMP_S  = 30
    AUTO_EST_RAMP_KB = 10
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 560
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_OBSTACLE
#define DBF_OBST
#define DBF_OBSTSESS
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_OBSTACLE
    ' SESSION 3, about 60 s planned: LEAD_IN_MS 10 s; two trials of about 10 s each (the ~1.3 s start, the drive to the obstacle
    '  0.3-0.8 m ahead at 0.16 m/s, ~1.2 s to the latch, the phase window 0.7 s, the API checks ~1 s, EV_SETTLE_MS ~1 s, the trace's
    '  drain and records -- 8.6 and 8.3 s at the first floor visit); and after each a STAND CLEAR of FR_CLEAR_MS 5 s, the armed drive back
    '  (at most 0.8 m at 0.16 m/s, about 6 s with its ramps) and its event drain: about 12 s; 10 + 2 x (10 + 12) = 54 s, and a
    '  lag fault's recovery (FAULT_COOL_MS 5 s) in either trial. Two traces, about 120 KB each. The cap is three times the plan
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 60
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 250
    OBST_TRIAL_EST_S  = 22
    OBST_TRIAL_EST_KB = 125
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 180
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_OBST_COAST
#define DBF_OBST
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_OBST_COAST
    ' about 40 s planned: LEAD_IN_MS 10 s, the start ~1.5 s, the drive to the obstacle (0.3-0.8 m at 0.16 m/s, 2-5 s
    '  and its start ramp) and ~1.2 s to the latch, the phase window 0.7 s, the API checks ~1 s, EV_SETTLE_MS ~1 s, and
    '  the trace's drain (up to TRACE_EMIT_MAX lines) and records; one trace, about 120 KB
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 40
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 120
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 120
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_OBST_SHORT
#define DBF_OBST
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_OBST_SHORT
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 40                                     ' as OBST_COAST: the same trial, the stop shorting
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 120
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 120
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_GRAB
#define DBF_GRAB
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_GRAB
    ' about 45 s planned: LEAD_IN_MS 10 s, the start ~1.5 s, the drive (0.4 m free at 0.16 m/s, then the last 0.6 m held
    '  at about half speed: about 11 s, LOAD_LEG_MS bounds it), EV_SETTLE_MS ~1 s, the drain and records; one trace
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 45
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 120
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 135
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_FAULTRUN
#define DBF_FAULTRUN
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_FAULTRUN
    ' about 65 s planned: LEAD_IN_MS 10 s, the start ~1.5 s, 1 m out at 0.23 m/s (~6 s), FR_CLEAR_MS 5 s, the drive back to
    '  the fault and its capture (~7 s), the recovery (<= 2 s) and FAULT_COOL_MS 5 s, FR_CLEAR_MS 5 s, the drive on to the
    '  start (~7 s), the drain and records; one trace
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 65
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 120
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 200
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_SPIN_SLOW_RIGHT
#define DBF_SPINLEG
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_SPIN_SLOW_RIGHT
    ' about 25 s planned: LEAD_IN_MS 10 s, the start ~1.5 s, the leg (one turn at SLOW takes about 8.2 s, SPIN_LEG_MS
    '  bounds it) and the records. The SLOW and MEDIUM legs drain no trace: about 5 KB
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 25
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 5
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 75
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_SPIN_SLOW_LEFT
#define DBF_SPINLEG
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_SPIN_SLOW_LEFT
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 25                                     ' as SLOW_RIGHT
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 5
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 75
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_SPIN_MED_RIGHT
#define DBF_SPINLEG
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_SPIN_MED_RIGHT
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 20                                     ' as SLOW, the leg about 4 s shorter at MEDIUM
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 5
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 60
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_SPIN_MED_LEFT
#define DBF_SPINLEG
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_SPIN_MED_LEFT
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 20                                     ' as MED_RIGHT
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 5
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 60
#else
#ifdef FLOOR_ACT_SPIN_FAST_RIGHT
#define DBF_SPINLEG
    FLOOR_ACT      = FLA_SPIN_FAST_RIGHT
    ' the quarter: a leg of about 5 s (SRC_REV 74, two turns: a spin-up of 0.8 s, 422 - 40 - 31 ticks at 98 ticks/s, a stop of
    '  0.6 s; it was about 3 s for one turn), and its capture is drained as a trace (TRACE_EMIT_MAX lines, about 120 KB): about
    '  32 s with LEAD_IN_MS, the start and the drain
    FLOOR_EST_S    = 32
    FLOOR_EST_KB   = 120
